{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nreview={\n'action':'review','artifact_id':'e5908ee5b3fe4acba53bfe3c5a782bc5',\n'rationale':'Review the fixed version-1 check and trusted execution adcc1c901782418b971256e7f414647b as one legal history. The measured false-success comparison is complete; scope does not extend to consensus disagreement.',\n'review_items':[{\n'aspect':'checker_correspondence','status':'no_issue_found',\n'source_ids':['src-notify-contract','src-superseded-contract','src-runtime-assignment','src-runtime-completion','src-runtime-loop','src-runtime-spawn','src-runtime-transport-contract','src-runtime-trait','src-runtime-tokio-adapter','src-public-manual-leader','src-leader','src-follower','src-sync','src-read-classify','src-memory','src-build'],\n'rationale':'Requirement and applicability: claim-notify-correspondence v1 is a success-only implication derived from append_notify promising the submitted entry\\\\'s decided index. The Superseded documentation permits conservative failure when an entry might survive leadership change; it does not permit success for a different value. The fixed check uses unique submitted payload 101 and replacement payload 202, no batching, compaction, crashes or storage failures. Entry and snapshot types instantiate the public API; TestRuntime supplies ordinary Tokio spawn/sleep matching the repository adapter, without intercepting protocol state.\\\\n\\\\nLegal history and producer reachability: the fixed source builds three valid fresh instances, establishes leader 1 through generated Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync traffic, checks all accepted and decided extents are zero, then moves the live node into spawn_actor. The original future is created by one actual append_notify(101). Its two actual AcceptDecide messages are observed and dropped during node-1 isolation; independent reads confirm peers 2 and 3 have no accepted entries. Node 2 uses public manual leadership and obtains node 3\\\\'s promise before accepting replacement 202. The new quorum does not contain the original entry, so replacing its unchosen position is legal. Deferred Prepare and subsequent Promise/AcceptSync are delivered as generated, preserving retained per-link order; no incoming payload or storage state is manufactured. Core peers are driven within a finite prefix, and no liveness/deadline property is inferred from their tick frequency. No reconnect injection or duplicate delivery is required.\\\\n\\\\nObserved prefix and result: execution adcc1c901782418b971256e7f414647b contains admission event 22 with payload 101, origin_decided 0 and empty peers; event 31 follows actual round-2 quorum work and reports replacement 202 decided at end index 1; event 36 follows actual round-2 synchronization and a live actor read showing Decided(202), with the original call still pending. Event 38 records the awaited original future returning success=true, returned_index=1, and a post-completion public read reporting decided_value=202. The monitor matched all three prerequisites and found no parse errors or missing observations. Static prerequisite values are emitted only after assertions against actual messages and reads. The outcome is not inferred from process PASS.\\\\n\\\\nOracle and correlation: one operation label independently identifies this sole append_notify call and its awaited JoinHandle/oneshot result. No compared value or changing ballot is used as an identity filter. The admission alias is explicitly admission; the assertion compares the actual decided_value with admission.payload only when observed success is true. The returned value is an exclusive accepted end index because append_tracked records get_accepted_idx; reading suffix(k-1) therefore observes the corresponding log entry. For this witness k=1, the live public read contains Decided(202), so neither missing-read sentinel nor zero-index fallback contributes to the comparison. These observations all belong to the same live objects and schedule; there are no isolated producer fragments.\\\\n\\\\nMechanism and alternatives: incoming higher-ballot handling replaces the old unchosen log and updates decided metadata while the pending assignment remains recorded. run invokes drain_notifiers on a later tick. Its first match arm returns Ok for idx <= decided without checking the stored ballot; the later Superseded arm is bypassed. Quorum preservation protects already-selected history but did not require retaining a value held only by isolated node 1. An earlier notifier tick could return Superseded, which is allowed; the observed pending marker and later success establish the actual timing for this execution. Event and transport channels are drained, real timers run, and teardown follows observation. The test ends after the operation result and independent read, without requiring any conflicting cluster decision.',\n'counterevidence':[],\n'limitations':['Only the exercised unbatched local-origin notification and fixed three-node history are established. Remote assignment and batching variants remain independent.','The observed core consensus decision is consistently 202; this check does not establish a consensus-agreement violation.','The test establishes one admissible schedule, not frequency or inevitability under arbitrary timer and network schedules.','Crash recovery, persistence failures, compaction and reconfiguration are excluded.'],\n'report_title':'领导权切换后，追加通知错误确认了被替换的写入',\n'report_answer':'原领导者提交的 101 未到达其他副本；新领导者与另一副本在同一位置决定了 202。原节点同步后，101 的 append_notify 仍返回 Ok(1)，公开日志读取却为 Decided(202)。这是客户端成功通知与实际决定内容不对应，不是已观察到的共识分歧。'\n}],\n'feedback':{'ref_ids':['aaa4b601803146088adba458a414a811','b-runtime-notify','b-runtime-assign','f-runtime-assignment','adcc1c901782418b971256e7f414647b','e5908ee5b3fe4acba53bfe3c5a782bc5','src-runtime-completion'],\n'answered':'The fixed legal history reached the original discriminator: an assignment fo